<h2>Links and Cross-Vault References</h2>
<p>Obsidian's greatest strength is <strong>links between notes</strong>. For example, a "BM25" note has all sorts of notes linked to it — an MOC (Map of Content, a knowledge map), harness engineering, logs, and more. These <strong>links are the heart of it</strong>.</p>

<h3>One address reads the linked knowledge along with it</h3>
<p>Hand artificial intelligence just the address of the "BM25" note, and it reads <strong>the rest of the notes linked to it, strung together like sausages</strong>. That automatic linking, however, only works <strong>within the same vault</strong>.</p>

